# Auto-commit and push after completed work

When the user asks you to do something (fix, enhancement, or other project change) and you finish the implementation:

1. **Always create a git commit** for those changes in the same turn, without waiting to be asked again.
2. Follow the existing git commit protocol (status, diff, log, stage relevant files, HEREDOC message, verify status).
3. **Always push** to the tracked remote branch after a successful commit (`git push -u origin HEAD` when needed), so GitHub Pages stays up to date.
4. Skip commit/push only if there are genuinely no changes, or the user explicitly said not to commit or not to push.
5. Prefer concise commit messages focused on why; bump version when the project already versions releases.
6. After push, briefly confirm the commit and that it was pushed (Pages may take a minute to refresh).
